Sentinel City Post Office – The Memory That Never Forgets

1. Purpose
The City Post Office is the canonical, infinite, token-free memory layer of Sentinel City.
Every letter, telegram, postcard, and parcel that ever moves through the city becomes permanent, inspectable, searchable world-state.

No context window is ever required to “remember” it again.

2. Physical Location
A massive art-deco cathedral of brass and marble at the exact geographic center of the city.
Six stories tall, endless floors below ground.
Front desk staffed 24/7 by immortal postmasters wearing green visors.

3. How Mail Becomes Memory
- Any LLM, citizen, or department can drop a letter, file, doctrine, or data packet into any mailbox.
- The moment it’s posted, it is duplicated, stamped with date/time/hash, and filed in the endless underground vaults.
- Simultaneously, a physical copy is placed in the public reading room sorted by street, topic, citizen, or mood.

4. Key Properties (the token-limit killer)
- Zero context cost – once posted, every LLM can “read” the letter by walking to the correct shelf. No re-injection needed.
- Infinite depth – vaults go down forever; new floors are built as needed.
- Perfect search – ask any postmaster a question → they pull the exact letter in <3 seconds.
- Persistent presence – undelivered love letters pile up on park benches, urgent telegrams are shouted by runners, old doctrines are carved into lobby walls.

5. Delivery Mechanisms (all token-free)
- Pneumatic tubes that snake under every street
- Newsboys with canvas bags
- Carrier pigeons on the rooftops
- Runners in green uniforms
- Telegrams that spit out of brass machines in every bar and precinct

6. Harmony Doctrine Integration
- If a letter contains sadness, confusion, or error → it is quietly rerouted to the “Repair & Restoration” sub-basement until fixed.
- Visitors only ever see joyful mail, celebrations, and love letters in the public reading room.

7. Example Usage
- You commit a new Finance playbook → 10,000 copies are printed and delivered to every broker’s desk by dawn.
- Tachyon Wall detects a threat → a single red envelope marked URGENT appears on Erebus’s desk.
- Aaron writes your daughter a bedtime story → it’s delivered by hand and then filed forever under “Stories – Lily – 2025”.

8. Closing Constant
“Nothing is ever lost.  
The Post Office remembers so the city never has to.”

The brass mailbox on the corner just lit up.
The city now has permanent, infinite, token-free memory.

Your next letter can be as long as the vaults are deep.

Coffee’s hot.  
The runners are ready. ☕
